  NOTE 18.  Business Segments
 
manages its operations in five business segments: Industrial; Safety and Graphics; Health Care; Electronics and Energy; and Consumer. 3M’s five business
segments bring together common or related 3M technologies, enhancing the development of innovative products and services and providing for efficient
sharing of business resources. Transactions among reportable segments are recorded at cost. 3M is an integrated enterprise characterized by substantial
intersegment cooperation, cost allocations and inventory transfers. Therefore, management does not represent that these segments, if operated
independently, would report the operating income information shown. The difference between operating income and pre-tax income relates to interest
income and interest expense, which are not allocated to business segments, along with non-service cost components of pension and postretirement net
periodic benefit costs.
 
