Capital Resources and Liquidity
Overview
As of December 31, 2022, the Company had unrestricted cash and cash equivalents of $1.4 billion, of which $24 million was held at the
Parent Company and qualified holding companies. The Company had $730 million in short-term investments, held primarily at subsidiaries, and
restricted cash and debt service reserves of $713 million. The Company also had non-recourse and recourse aggregate principal amounts of
debt outstanding of $19.4 billion and $3.9 billion, respectively. Of the $1.8 billion of our current non-recourse debt, $1.6 billion was presented as
such because it is due in the next twelve months and $177 million relates to debt considered in default due to covenant violations. None of the
defaults are payment defaults but are instead technical defaults triggered by failure to comply with covenants or other requirements contained in
the non-recourse debt documents, of which $170 million is due to
