ANSWER:
The key agenda of Amcor plc's Form 8-K filing dated July 1, 2022, was to report the substitution of Amcor Flexibles North America, Inc. (the “Substitute Issuer”) for Amcor Finance (USA), Inc. (the “Former Issuer”) and the assumption by the Substitute Issuer of the covenants of the Former Issuer under the 2016 Indenture and the 2019 Indenture.

This was executed on June 30, 2022, through the following:
*   **Second Supplemental Indenture:** Relating to the 2016 Indenture governing the Former Issuer’s (a) 3.625% Guaranteed Senior Notes due 2026 and (b) 4.500% Guaranteed Senior Notes due 2028.
*   **First Supplemental Indenture:** Relating to the 2019 Indenture governing the Former Issuer’s (a) 3.625% Guaranteed Senior Notes due 2026 and (b) 4.500% Guaranteed Senior Notes due 2028.

GOLD:
Amcor Finance (USA), Inc. and Amcor Flexibles North America, Inc., entered into supplemental indentures relating to Guaranteed Senior Notes due 2026 and 2028. This involved the substitution of the Substitute Issuer (Amcor Flexibles North America) for the Former Issuer (Amcor Finance) and the assumption of covenants under the indentures. (In essence a novation agreement)

