In 2020, cash flows used in investing activities increased $116 million primarily due to continued investment across all infrastructure categories, mainly
replacement and renewal of transmission and distribution and treatment and pumping infrastructure in the Company’s Regulated Businesses, as discussed below.
Additionally, proceeds from the sale of assets were higher in 2019 compared to 2020, due to the sale of Keystone for $31 million, in the fourth quarter of 2019.
