We account for business combinations under the acquisition method of accounting. This method requires the recording of acquired assets and assumed liabilities 
at their acquisition date fair values. The excess of the purchase price over the fair value of assets acquired and liabilities assumed is recorded as 
goodwill. Results of operations related to business combinations are included prospectively beginning with the date of acquisition and transaction costs related to 
business combinations are recorded within SG&A.
