institutions and, consequently, an increase in leverage 
exposure and the GSIB surcharge
•
changes in the composition of JPMorgan Chase’s 
balance sheet or developments that could increase 
RWA, such as increased market risk, customer 
delinquencies, client credit rating downgrades or other 
factors, and
•
increases in estimated stress losses as determined by 
the Federal Reserve under the Comprehensive Capital 
Analysis and Review, which could increase JPMorgan 
Chase’s SCB.
