For fiscal 2018, our consolidated gross margin was 80 basis points lower than fiscal 2017, primarily reflecting the following factors:
•
Unfavorable changes in net foreign currency exchange rates, including hedges (decreasing gross margin approximately 90 basis points);
•
Lower NIKE Direct margin (decreasing gross margin approximately 10 basis points) reflecting higher mix of off-price sales in the first half of fiscal 2018, which was
partially offset by margin expansion in the second half of fiscal 2018;
•
NIKE Brand full-price ASP, net of discounts, on a wholesale equivalent basis, which was flat for fiscal 2018 as higher discounts in the first half of fiscal 2018 were
offset by higher full-price ASP in the second half of the year; and
•
NIKE Brand product costs, on a wholesale equivalent basis, which were flat.
