write-offs of approximately $300 million in the second quarter and $240 million in the first six months for Comirnaty inventory that exceeded or was
expected to exceed its approved shelf-life prior to being used; and
• a reduction of $1.0 billion in the second quarter and $630 million in the first six months due to lower sales of Paxlovid.
